  "question": {
    "text": "Two thin wires rings each having a radius $R$ are placed at a distance $d$ apart with their axes coinciding. The charges on the two rings are $+q$ and $-q$. The potential difference between the centres of the two rings is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Iw2EW",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{QR} / 4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{~d}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1VuWV",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{Q}{2 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\left[\\frac{1}{R}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{R^2+d^2}}\\right]$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "X9xNa",
      "text": "\nzero\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "osAyu",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\left[\\frac{1}{R}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{R^2+d^2}}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$v_1=\\frac{k q}{R}-\\frac{k q}{\\sqrt{R^2+d^2}}$\n$v_2=\\frac{-k q}{R}+\\frac{k q}{\\sqrt{R^2+d^2}}$",
